 bribery case\". *India Today*. Retrieved 5 October 2017.\n74. ↑ \"IPS officer gets 13-year jail term for pilfering seized drug\". *Daily News and Analysis*. 11 March 2013. Retrieved 5 October 2017.\n75. ↑ \"Corruption case against IPS officer, 5 held by Vigilance Dept\". *The Hindu*. 23 June 2016. Retrieved 5 October 2017.\n76. ↑ Sood, Aman (18 August 2016). \"Booked for job fraud, IPS officer on the run\". *The Tribune*. Retrieved 5 October 2017.\n77. ↑ \"HC clears trial of officer who flew family around the world in Rs 1 lakh\". *Mumbai Mirror*. 17 September 2013.\n78. ↑ \"This Delhi cop is a 'corrupt crorepati' - 17 shell companies, 11 posh properties and much more\". *Times Now*. 19 September 2017.\n79. ↑ \"Punjab has a new enemy to fight in war on drugs: Punjab Police\". *The Print*. 3 June 2018.\n80. ↑ Qadri, Afzal (1994). \"Police Corruption: An Analysis\". *Indian Journal of Criminology*. **22**.\n81. ↑ Lamani, Ravikanth Babu (2013). \"Police Corruption in India\". *International Journal of Criminology and Sociological Theory*. **6**.\n82. ↑ Lamba, Jonika; Jain, Esha (8 February 2023). \"A Study on Police Accountability and Custodial Violence in India\". *IARS' International Research Journal*. **13** (01). doi:10.51611/iars.irj.v13i01.2023.227. ISSN 1839-6518.\n83. ↑ Journal, IJLLR (26 June 2025). \"Custodial Violence In India: A Legal And Human Rights Perspective\". *IJLLR Journal*. Retrieved 1 December 2025.\n84. ↑ \"Broken System — Dysfunction, Abuse, and Impunity in the Indian Police\" (PDF). *Human Rights Watch*. 2009. ISBN 1564325180. Retrieved 30 November 2025.\n85. ↑ *Status of Policing in India Report 2025 — Police Torture and (Un)Accountability* (PDF). Delhi: Common Cause & Lokniti – Centre for the Study of Developing Societies (CSDS). 2025.\n86. ↑ \"Andhra Pradesh extends suspension of IPS officer accused of corruption\". *India Today*. 1 February 2025. Retrieved 1 December 2025.\n87. ↑ M, Sambasiva Rao (25 December 2024). \"ACB files case against IPS officer N. Sanjay in Andhra Pradesh\". *The Hindu*. ISSN 0971-751X. Retrieved 1 December 2025.\n88. ↑ \"Andhra Pradesh: Suspension Of IPS Officer Sanjay Extended For Another Six Months\". *Deccan Chronicle*. 28 May 2025. Retrieved 1 December 2025.\n89. ↑ Naveen (4 September 2025). \"IPS Officer Sanjay Grilled by ACB in Major Corruption Probe\". *NewKerala.com*. Retrieved 1 December 2025.\n90. ↑ Livemint (23 June 2025). \"Who is IPS officer Gaurav Upadhyay accused of assaulting 14-yr-old in Assam? 'Force to kiss, touched private parts' | Today News\". *mint*. Retrieved 1 December 2025.\n91. ↑ PTI (21 June 2025). \"Special court in Assam orders framing of charges under POCSO, IPC against IPS officer\". *The Hindu*. ISSN 0971-751X. Retrieved 1 December 2025.\n92. Jump up to: 1 2 \"Government allows women to be combat officers in all Central Armed Police Forces\". *The Economic Times*. 11 July 2018. Archived from the original on 24 February 2019. Retrieved 11 March 2019.\n93. ↑ \"Women quota in CRPF, CISF to be made 15 per cent\". *telegraphindia.com*. Archived from the original on 3 April 2019. Retrieved 11 March 2019.\n94. ↑ \"First woman IPS officer Kiran Bedi seeks voluntary retirement\". *The Economic Times*. 27 November 2007. Retrieved 18 September 2017.\n95. ↑ \"First ever woman chief of SSB retires; Rajni Kant Mishra takes charge\". *Economic Times*. 14 July 2018.\n96. ↑ \"Kanpur and Agra gets new IG range, 12 IPS officers transferred\". 27 October 2021.\n97. ↑ Shihab, Siam (15 October 2023). \"Nina Singh IPS Wiki, Biography, Age, Height, Husband, Career, Networth & Facts\". *EXPOSE BD*. Retrieved 29 December 2023.\n98. ↑ \"Nina Singh to be first woman chief of CISF\". *The Times of India*. 29 December 2023. ISSN 0971-8257. Retrieved 29 December 2023.\n\n## Further reading\n\n[edit]\n\n* *History of services of Indian police service, as on 1 July 1966*, by Ministry of Home Affairs, India. Published by the Government of India, 1969.\n* *The peace keepers: Indian Police Service (IPS)*, by S. R. Arun, IPS, DGP Uttar Pradesh. Published by Berghahn Books, 2000. ISBN 978-81-7049-107-1.\n* *The Indian Police Journal (IPJ)*, by Bureau of Police Research and Development, Ministry of Home Affairs. Published by the Government of India, October–December 2009 Vol.LVI-No.4. ISSN 0537-2429.\n* *History of services of Indian police service, as on 1 July 1966*, by Ministry of Home Affairs, India. Published by the Government of India, 1969.\n\n## External links\n\n[edit]\n\nWikimedia Commons has media related to Indian Police Service.\n\n* Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel National Police Academy\n* \"Shortage of IPS officers\". Press Information Bureau. Archived from the original on 30 December 2016.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":6803.6995349999925,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}